<title>USA: Union approves Briggs &amp; Stratton contract.</title>
<headline>Union approves Briggs &amp; Stratton contract.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Briggs &amp; Stratton Corp said Wednesday that members of Local 7232 of the United Paperworkers International Union approved a new contract with the company that runs into the year 2002.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said the new contract includes wage increases totaling 10 percent over the life of the pact in addition to certain work rule changes.</p>
<p>The company said the contract replaces a pact that expires in August of 1998 and covers about 3,000 employees at the Briggs &amp; Stratton plant in Milwaukee.</p>
<p>Briggs &amp; Stratton makes air-cooled gasoline engines.</p>
<p>Its shares closed down 3/8 Wednesday at 44-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
